\import{base-macros}

\p{\code{\verb~|unsafe_data_ptr~} returns a \code{\verb~|ConstPtr<core::ptr::Generic>~} to the first byte or element: \code{\verb~|core::intrinsic::str::unsafe_data_ptr~} and \code{\verb~|core::intrinsic::array::unsafe_data_ptr~} for the builtin types, and a member of \code{\verb~|String~}, \code{\verb~|Vec~}, \code{\verb~|Text~} and \code{\verb~|TextView~}. The pointer keeps nothing alive. See [data pointers](design-opaque-pointers-data-pointers). \pr{992}.}
